It is built on OOTRR, the Ocarina of Time remake randomizer by REALAZK and contributors
(https://github.com/realazk/ootrr), licensed GPL-3.0-or-later:
- src/engine.js ports OOTRR's logic engine (crates/core/src: rule_ast.rs, rules.rs, world.rs, search.rs).
- src/seed.js ports its settings string and seed file reading (settings/codec.rs, settings/string.rs,
  settings/seed.rs) and the settings-to-logic mapping (slice/support.rs, start_items/give.rs).
- src/autotrack.js ports its save reading and tracker rules (tracker/peek.rs, tracker/rules.rs,
  tracker/grid.rs, tracker/seed.rs, murmur.rs).
- data/data.json is generated from OOTRR 0.6.2's data files and an export of ootrr-core
  (tools/ootrr-export), so it carries OOTRR's logic, settings schema, locations and tracker targets.

OOTRR's logic engine follows the design of the OoT Randomizer (https://github.com/OoTRandomizer/OoT-Randomizer,
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 OoTRandomizer), and its logic files come from the OoT Randomizer.
Credit to AmazingAmpharos, Testrunner, Zannick, Junglechief87 and the other OoT Randomizer contributors.

tools/live/ootrr-live.ps1 (the Longshot live helper) reads the game's memory with the layout documented
by OotrR (https://github.com/Mozencaz/OotrR, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Mozencaz;
src/oot_rando/tracker/live_memory.py): the GameData slot and Bool table, which follow Hookshot's own
cheat menu, the Bool64bitKey records from the sloperina practice menu, and the way emulators are found
(MOD0 modules near 0x80000000). The helper's code is the tracker's own.

No game files or game assets are included. Item tiles are text.
